A||||4||Larry Miller||Heater core change
Z||000000||Larry Miller||05-05-99||04:50 PM||||What all is involved in changing out a heater core in a 84 with AC? Mine was leaking, but did a temporary fix by by-passing the heater core. Any advice?
Z||000001||Punkndrublic||05-05-99||07:17 PM||||I had to change heater(was leaking into the passenger side through the vents) so maybe this will help, but I have no A/C. I m guessing it should be basically the same way if the A/C doesn't get in the way. I drained some coolant out of the car, then disconected the heater core lines. Have some rags or towels handy cause the lines might leak when you disconnect them then i just move them out of the way. Took off the front of the heater/fan box. I left most of the wires and stuff on and just "folded" it up and put it on the wipers, then theres a screw and a metal plate that holds done one side of the heater core, slide it out remove the core put in the new one.I had a little trouble here, the core didn't slide in as easily as the old one came out, just make sure the back part goes under the metal clips that hold the back part done. All the air passages had collect coolant so I made sure to clean them all out. Then put everything back together again. I ve never seen an A/C setup real close so it might get in the way. But otherwise the hardest part for me was that the coolant lines were stuck on. I cut just enough off to pull them off, and there was enough slack left to re-attach them without replacing them. Another thing is get a new heater core from a local rad shop, I paid $70 cdn for mine and thats with 14 % tax on it, compared to the 79 us at the fiero store before taxes and shipping.
Z||000002||Yellow85||05-15-99||12:29 PM||||I got my core for $20 CAN from junk yard!!<br>It only took me about 10 min to replace it.<br>
Z||000003||Punkndrublic||05-16-99||10:39 AM||||Well i would have done that but i didn't like the idea when coolant started leaking through my vents and pooling on the passenger side, this way its brand new and i won't have that happen again for a long time.
Z||000004||Gokart||05-19-99||07:24 PM||||Good advice not to fool at the junk yard with something like a heater core!Took me about an hour to do mine. Didn't have to drain any coolant, just clamped off both hoses with needle nose vise grips. The hardest part was getting the hoses off the leaking one, can't get any leveridge or prying action because of its local. Just have patience!
